% M18-coverage-T14 / D-0247: a scene where a HOLE decides a global_cardinality count bound.
% Route (a) of D-0247 (rule C and rule (b) of lib/core/prop/gcc.ml reading holes, each cited
% through the entry that punched it) was built, verified on these models, measured over the
% Challenge's variable-count instances and NOT kept: it lost on score (branch commit d94f08f).
% The models stay as proof-checked regressions of the native propagator on hole scenes; the
% std decomposition that variable counts now reach through mznlib reads holes by itself.
% OPT. Two cover values share one count; the branch w = 2 is bounded by holes under a decision.
var 1..4: w :: output_var;
var 1..4: x1 :: output_var;
var 1..4: x2 :: output_var;
var 1..4: x3 :: output_var;
var 1..4: x4 :: output_var;
var 0..4: n :: output_var;
constraint int_ne(x1,w);
constraint int_ne(x2,w);
constraint int_ne(x3,w);
constraint int_ne(x4,3);
constraint fzn_global_cardinality([x1,x2,x3,x4],[2,3],[n,n]);
solve :: int_search([w,x1,x2,x3,x4], input_order, indomain_median) maximize n;
